values ('b0c1d2e3-4f5a-4b35-8e45-5c6d7e8f9a85', 'islam', 'Islam', 'Study Islam academically, respectfully, and critically through texts, rituals, histories, communities, objects, law, theology, and modern public life. The course situates early Islam in late antiquity, then covers the Qur''an and tafsir, Muhammad and the early community, hadith and legal schools, ritual and ethical practice, Sunni and Shi''i traditions, theology and philosophy, Sufism, empires and institutions, knowledge and material culture, gender and family, global and diaspora Islam, modern reform and state power, and contemporary public scholarship.');

