 Canadian, European, Caribbean, and Latin American Muslim communities"}], "description": "Students examine how Islam is lived under migration and pluralism."}]}, {"id": "5b1f0569-2c20-4897-b338-53132de9ac3f", "type": "topic", "title": "Modern Reform, Colonialism, Nationalism, Secularism, Islamism, and State Power", "description": "This module analyzes modern transformations of Islam through colonial rule, reform movements, nation-states, secularism, political Islam, and global power.", "children": [{"id": "0816443d-61c1-41e3-b4e7-b4c2aefbb8fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Colonialism and reform", "children": [{"id": "0b7305c6-10ac-4501-ac83-beda38554200", "type": "concept", "title": "European imperialism, missionary critique, Orientalism, print, education, codified law, and reform"}, {"id": "3f80be8e-f4ee-495d-b032-940e6f40b3c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Modernism, Salafism, revivalism, anti-colonialism, and pan-Islam"}, {"id": "6790f52d-1b2f-4819-b300-0ee6655845e3", "type": "concept", "title": "al-Afghani, Muhammad Abduh, Rashid Rida, Iqbal, and regional reformers"}], "description": "Students learn how modern power reshaped Muslim institutions and debates."}, {"id": "2ac3f853-0308-4fd9-abdf-a5b2b4d301cb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nation-states and secularism", "children": [{"id": "809d72cb-19ad-4751-9b61-8cf5466bf1f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Turkey, Iran, Egypt, Saudi Arabia, Pakistan, Indonesia, and other state models"}, {"id": "ad2efa73-988f-4508-8d3f-9630d9cb4e84", "type": "concept", "title": "Constitutions, personal status law, religious ministries, courts, parties, and education"}, {"id": "a9a7bff7-8619-4576-9281-ca7fe9fd427e", "type": "concept", "title": "Nationalism, citizenship, minorities, and state control"}], "description": "The gist is to analyze religion and politics beyond simple secular/religious binaries."}, {"id": "bed76f69-d93e-4667-a926-fccffb037490", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Islamism and political movements", "children": [{"id": "549c7287-a08c-4a5a-8887-e6c3a53b9f7c", "type": "concept", "title": "Muslim Brotherhood, Jamaat-e-Islami, Iranian Revolution, political parties, activism, and militancy"}, {"id": "0b78f153-f04e-49f6-9e26-c70fa985f2a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Secularism, democracy, authoritarianism, violence, and social welfare"}, {"id": "5e209c6a-94f4-4750-8f3c-667bb4cdd3bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Media narratives, policy categories, and ethical analysis"}], "description": "Students distinguish movements, ideologies, and contexts carefully."}]}, {"id": "d622b9dd-e31c-4cbe-9262-5d33630aa9c8", "type": "topic", "title": "Contemporary Islam and Comparative Capstone: Pluralism, Media, Ethics, and Public Scholarship", "description": "Students synthesize the course by researching a contemporary issue, community, text, practice, or public controversy using careful evidence and respectful interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "734deb3b-2ba6-46cc-91dc-af4b167dc8ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contemporary public issues", "children": [{"id": "7a093de6-49b9-4a32-b1ff-cc0a093ef1fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Pluralism, interfaith work, law, education, finance, climate, health, gender, anti-Muslim racism, and public policy"}, {"id": "005e6d7b-9523-417d-9b62-c8c580471537", "type": "concept", "title": "Muslim minorities and majorities"}, {"id": "f7aa3c78-c44c-40ce-bc4c-190a6285a9a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Local community study and global comparison"}], "description": "Students connect course knowledge to current debates without flattening Muslim diversity."}, {"id": "5cb83c10-ec1f-4292-a41b-c64dfc19acda", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media and digital Islam", "children": [{"id": "f92c0dc4-abdf-47d8-ae14-02d00b030aee", "type": "concept", "title": "Satellite television, podcasts, YouTube, social media, apps, online fatwas, and digital Qur'an tools"}, {"id": "abf31fd6-fadd-422a-b8e8-d1ea8047dbc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Influencers, scholars, institutions, publics, and misinformation"}, {"id": "ed83a811-872c-41d3-af02-bc27001d6657", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodiment, ritual, privacy, and community online"}], "description": "The point is to understand how authority and practice move through contemporary media."}, {"id": "03c31949-b3d7-42c2-a734-efb68eccc9ff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capstone research and public scholarship", "children": [{"id": "6fd5d606-51b5-411b-bf58-265c0958bb4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Research question, annotated bibliography, primary source or field evidence, and thesis"}, {"id": "161fecc3-03dd-4066-8385-04123f3d86f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Public-facing output: exhibit label, policy brief, podcast script, teaching guide, or digital essay"}, {"id": "4577dc50-9a28-47cf-a982-32a371cb2863", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics, citation, positionality, and respectful representation"}], "description": "Students synthesize skills in a responsible final project."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$isljson$::jsonb,
